  "body": "**Replaces #429** (opened from the old fork, which can no longer take pushes). Same head commit; nothing else changed.\n\n## What changed\nWhile a setup's settings page is open and its stock source is \"What <previous setup> leaves behind\", the viewport draws the incoming body as a translucent **teal** sheet, in the active setup's frame, distinct from the setup's own Stock node.\n\n- App: new `setup_stock_view::incoming_shape(world, setup)` calls `stock_sim::incoming_body` once and returns the box/volume plus `body.display().surface(&[])` as triangles mapped into the viewport's frame (`A_active * inverse(A_setup)`; identity when the setup is active). An empty body or sheet is an error naming the setup; a bad index is skipped, never a panic.\n- UI: `incoming_view::IncomingView` caches it keyed by (setup, active setup, `doc_version`) - measured once per document version, never per frame - refreshed at the end of `drain_actions` and cleared the moment the page closes, another page opens, or the setup switches to its own stock. A failed measurement is logged once and draws nothing.\n- Drawing: `collect_parts` adds a stock-type part with vertex class 4; `fs_stock` paints class 4 as teal rgb (0.12, 0.66, 0.74) at alpha 0.45 in the existing translucent stock pass.\n- The page's incoming box/volume text reuses the viewport's measurement, so there is one program sim per version instead of two.\n- Display only: no command, nothing undoable (ephemeral view state per AGENTS.md). No files #412 touches were edited (`stock_sim*.rs`, `operation/*`, `rest/*`).\n\n## Readings\nDebug, M5 Mac. `scripts/gate.sh quick` (camcraft-app + camcraft-ui suites): 1718 passed, 4 failed - all known reds on main (`setup_stock_source::a_new_block_after_a_flip…` #415; GPU headless trio). Clippy `-D warnings` clean. The changed WGSL shader was validated offline with naga 30.0.1; the `gpu_render` tests skip here (no adapter in the sandbox).\n\n## Pinning tests\n- UI lib `egui_app::incoming_view_tests`: `the_incoming_stock_shows_while_the_carried_setups_page_is_open` (real properties pane via egui_kittest: one class-4 part with Setup2's page open, top at Z 16 where Setup1 faced to; measured once, three more frames measure nothing, a `doc_version` bump measures once more; Close removes it), `no_incoming_stock_for_own_stock_or_another_page`.\n- App `crates/app/tests/setup_stock_view.rs`: `the_sheet_stands_in_the_active_setups_frame`, `the_first_setup_draws_its_own_block_and_an_unknown_setup_is_named`.\n\n## Not exercised\nNo real-GPU render of the teal and no hand GUI run yet - **draft until the GUI check**. Known limit: the traced whole-program stock view replaces all stock-type parts, so the overlay hides with it. Posted G-code unchanged.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/406-incoming-stock-preview.md`.\n\nChangelog: The setup page previews the incoming (carried) stock in the viewport as a translucent teal body while a setup that takes what the previous setup leaves behind is open\n\nFixes #406\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
